  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Impact Cluster: HortiBenin</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This three-year (2020-2023) project aims to create a resilient and competitive horticulture sector in Benin that contributes to the national gross domestic product (GDP) and provides jobs and income for youth and women smallholders, while contributing to food security and an increased supply of healthy vegetables on the local market.At the same time, Dutch small- and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) and companies will introduce their quality seeds, irrigation, processing techniques and hardware in Benin and establish business activities in Benin&apos;s horticultural sector.By introducing Dutch know-how and innovative technologies, this impact cluster will contribute to the development of the local horticulture sector by training 40 lead farmers so as to improve their production techniques (including access to quality seeds), processing and storage capacities, commercial and financial skills. Each lead farmer will then train ten other farmers in their community through demo plots on their farm.In addition, entrepreneurial skills training will be introduced in two Technical and Vocational Education and Trainings (TVETs) in the North and South of Benin and five cooperatives strengthened in governance and business activities.Local partner Les Primeurs du Benin will facilitate market access and manage the outgrower scheme of the lead farmers of cooperatives the cluster works with.</narrative>
  </description>
